Of course, one doesn't have to do Sokoban. Leaving it alone, however,
brings the penalty of missing out on rings, wands, and the Prize At
The End. I suppose the devteam could choose to reward those who
like--or at least are willing-- to do puzzles. But it's worth noting
that the existing datafile comments apply to the existing Sokoban,
which can be learned relatively quickly; not to a hypothetical one
which would offer something approaching a new set of puzzles every
game.

Maybe there could be ways to get around the puzzles (as there are ways
to get around the Castle drawbridge), which would offer drawbacks to
compensate for the advantage of not having to do the puzzles. (Of
course, I suppose these exist now--the drawbacks coming in the form of
luck penalties.)
